} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370039}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2fcc379f-2f4b-5f54-bdd5-04d5716c1760" :question/math-academy-id "q-104909" :question/problem "If $A={1,{10,12},15,{22,26,28},{42,62}}$, then $|A|=$" :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $A:$\n\n$$\n1,\\,{10,12},\\,15,\\,{22,26,28},\\,{42,62}\n$$\n\nNote that ${10,12},$ ${22,26,28},$ and ${42,62}$ each count as single elements of $A.$\n\nSince $A$ has $5$ elements, the cardinality is $|A|=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054987 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebc025a5-9c66-5ddc-a12c-42595f905c17" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Geometric Sequences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d61fcce4-b1cc-5f5e-a928-d38d216bb0ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370045} {:answer/id #uuid "75f89d73-cb7b-5fd4-9d9f-085022d3ab34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370046}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d61fcce4-b1cc-5f5e-a928-d38d216bb0ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370045} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2801469-fcbb-52a5-b26b-9773c73cabba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051845}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d64c45b7-2d40-58ad-9748-05e941de30d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-181454" :question/problem "If $A={3,6,12,24,48,…,98\\,304},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n3,\\,6,\\,12,\\,24,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =2 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{6} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our geometric sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1}=3({2}^{n-1})=\\frac{3}{2}(2)^{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nA={\\frac{3}{2}(2)^{n}:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}(2)^{N} & =98\\,304 \\\\ {2}^{N} & =65\\,536 \\\\ N & ={log}_{2}⁡(65\\,536) \\\\ N & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡(65\\,536)}{{log}_{10}⁡(2)} \\\\ N & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={\\frac{3}{2}(2)^{n}:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 16}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $16$ elements, we must have $|A|=16.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370047 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb35fcff-d9f0-5ae8-999e-7e8bbc0b0919" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cardinality of a Finite Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff512eba-85e2-54cd-b236-cd8c6e78d355" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff512eba-85e2-54cd-b236-cd8c6e78d355" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370049} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d84293b-f344-5cf0-a3be-552d58049f5c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370048}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e785a181-80ef-535b-a367-3a898de69e5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-181547" :question/problem "If $S={\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{3},\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{7}},$ then $|S|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $S$ is the number of elements in $S.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{2},\\,\\sqrt{3},\\,\\sqrt{5},\\,\\sqrt{7}\n$$\n\nSince $S$ has $4$ elements, its cardinality is $|S|=\\text{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306087 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb35fcff-d9f0-5ae8-999e-7e8bbc0b0919" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cardinality of a Finite Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d5ac7f2-4727-542b-97f5-91ade2a1301c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306089} {:answer/id #uuid "b9f0ffc4-d5fa-51ff-ad89-b88e391e4b6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d5ac7f2-4727-542b-97f5-91ade2a1301c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306089} :answer-field/id #uuid "146a0fb6-b5f9-578e-a298-762346302c0f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306088}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "194441f2-444c-55a9-a85f-5412a54a2464" :question/math-academy-id "q-181551" :question/problem "If $C={5,10,15,…,40},$ then $|C|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $C$ is the number of elements in $C.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $C:$\n\n$$\n5,\\,10,\\,15,\\,20,\\,25,\\,30,\\,35,\\,40\n$$\n\nSince $C$ has $8$ elements, its cardinality is $|C|=\\text{8}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306090 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb35fcff-d9f0-5ae8-999e-7e8bbc0b0919" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cardinality of a Finite Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1c00dd5-25c5-51c5-ac52-871fd08895f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306092}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1c00dd5-25c5-51c5-ac52-871fd08895f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306092} :answer-field/id #uuid "a33cbb1e-0cfb-5292-bd74-6790cc9d240b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306091}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "81299303-dc1c-515b-b89c-175532d2eeb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-181553" :question/problem "If $X={a,c,a,b,a,b,d}$, then $|X|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $X$ is the number of elements in $X.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $X:$\n\n$$\na,\\,b,\\,c,\\,d\n$$\n\nNote that only *unique* elements are counted. In other words, duplicate elements are *not* counted separately.\n\nSince $X$ has $4$ elements, its cardinality is $|X|=\\text{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306093 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "24ce056e-1fe1-55d4-b88c-62629435003b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cardinality of a Set With Set Elements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe0b0813-21d9-52a2-8f85-afcbccc8b1eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306095} {:answer/id #uuid "8985779f-54e0-5594-89f8-6217877a8ca2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370051}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe0b0813-21d9-52a2-8f85-afcbccc8b1eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306095} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f3ddb3c-9f2c-53ce-a336-68b619092ee5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306094}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a605e37a-7d60-532f-958b-d76317ddbdf2" :question/math-academy-id "q-181557" :question/problem "If $T={0,{-2,-3,-4},{9,10,11,12}}$, then $|T|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $T$ is the number of elements in $T.$\n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $T:$\n\n$$\n0,\\,{-2,-3,-4},\\,{9,10,11,12}\n$$\n\nNote that ${-2,-3,-4}$ and ${9,10,11,12}$ each count as single elements of $T.$\n\nSince $T$ has $3$ elements, the cardinality is $|T|=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306096 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8374fcf7-6bb2-52a9-9949-20b50d7081b1" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Arithmetic Sequences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d1402c5-4acc-517b-957d-5e989e7f6bab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "315" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306098} {:answer/id #uuid "91361b35-1806-56a5-a47c-db4792c5aa9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "316" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306099}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91361b35-1806-56a5-a47c-db4792c5aa9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "316" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306099} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae666fef-4750-5c6e-be96-688bcbe5b75d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306097}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "49131e72-c8a0-59f3-99af-aa1dff260098" :question/math-academy-id "q-181559" :question/problem "If $A={15,21,27,…,1\\,905},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n15,\\,21,\\,27,\\,…\n$$\n\nform an arithmetic sequence with a common difference $d=6:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =6 \\\\  & =21-15 \\\\  & =27-21 \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =15+(n-1)\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =15+6n-6 \\\\  & =6n+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={6n+9:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6N+9 & =1\\,905 \\\\ 6N & =1\\,896 \\\\ N & =\\frac{1\\,896}{6} \\\\ N & =316\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={6n+9:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 316}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $316$ elements, we must have $|A|=316.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370052 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8374fcf7-6bb2-52a9-9949-20b50d7081b1" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Arithmetic Sequences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a790c782-9db3-5d30-9e7b-5d2b79eb784c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "179" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a790c782-9db3-5d30-9e7b-5d2b79eb784c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "179" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370054} :answer-field/id #uuid "0681fd81-d1a6-552e-9c6f-aa8dcac4d0ca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370053}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5d67bf8a-a51f-5a68-95c6-b3470ada6ae8" :question/math-academy-id "q-181561" :question/problem "If $A={98,102,106,…,810},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n98,\\,102,\\,106,\\,…\n$$\n\nform an arithmetic sequence with a common difference $d=4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =4 \\\\  & =102-98 \\\\  & =106-102 \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =98+(n-1)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =98+4n-4 \\\\  & =4n+94.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={4n+94:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4N+94 & =810 \\\\ 4N & =716 \\\\ N & =\\frac{716}{4} \\\\ N & =179\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={4n+94:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 179}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $179$ elements, we must have $|A|=179.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054993 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8374fcf7-6bb2-52a9-9949-20b50d7081b1" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Arithmetic Sequences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81e53f55-af8d-51fb-a296-b63e29304373" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "172" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306103} {:answer/id #uuid "0a3e3c04-33bc-5e83-8673-861763310039" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "171" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370055}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81e53f55-af8d-51fb-a296-b63e29304373" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "172" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306103} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f183342-6bfa-5336-98cc-06e7ffe19937" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051856}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c9e87e7b-6e84-5dd8-a2d8-4ac3f8e8903d" :question/math-academy-id "q-181563" :question/problem "If $A={-200,-193,-186,…,997},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n-200,\\,-193,\\,-186,\\,…\n$$\n\nform an arithmetic sequence with a common difference $d=7:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =7 \\\\  & =-193-(-200) \\\\  & =-186-(-193) \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-200+(n-1)\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =-200+7n-7 \\\\  & =7n-207.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={7n-207:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7N-207 & =997 \\\\ 7N & =1\\,204 \\\\ N & =\\frac{1\\,204}{7} \\\\ N & =172\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={7n-207:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 172}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $172$ elements, we must have $|A|=172.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370056 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8374fcf7-6bb2-52a9-9949-20b50d7081b1" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Arithmetic Sequences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca7fe877-2e4b-5b33-902f-eac0d170d910" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1172" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370058} {:answer/id #uuid "6b939c76-c6b4-54db-a953-2861a40252c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1171" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370059}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca7fe877-2e4b-5b33-902f-eac0d170d910" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1172" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370058} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e99bfad-f453-5595-88cd-a12a8cd3134a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370057}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "359ce01e-7589-5ea5-9246-896c5271d8b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-181566" :question/problem "If $A={-875,-869,-863,…,6\\,151},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n-875,\\,-869,\\,-863,\\,…\n$$\n\nform an arithmetic sequence with a common difference $d=6:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =6 \\\\  & =-869-(-875) \\\\  & =-863-(-869) \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-875+(n-1)\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =-875+6n-6 \\\\  & =6n-881.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={6n-881:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6N-881 & =6\\,151 \\\\ 6N & =7\\,032 \\\\ N & =\\frac{7\\,032}{6} \\\\ N & =1\\,172\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={6n-881:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 1\\,172}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $1\\,172$ elements, we must have $|A|=1\\,172.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370060 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8374fcf7-6bb2-52a9-9949-20b50d7081b1" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Arithmetic Sequences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6840236d-565f-5bce-b2bc-e90bb8adfff6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2609" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370062}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6840236d-565f-5bce-b2bc-e90bb8adfff6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2609" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370062} :answer-field/id #uuid "a39118b0-5fdc-5c1a-b0e5-023f16d9c9b4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370061}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b7155e82-f133-5ff9-8973-883ba9513f97" :question/math-academy-id "q-181573" :question/problem "If $A={-615,-610,-605,…,12\\,425},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n-615,\\,-610,\\,-605,\\,…\n$$\n\nform an arithmetic sequence with a common difference $d=5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =5 \\\\  & =-610-(-615) \\\\  & =-605-(-610) \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-615+(n-1)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-615+5n-5 \\\\  & =5n-620.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={5n-620:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5N-620 & =12\\,425 \\\\ 5N & =13\\,045 \\\\ N & =\\frac{13\\,045}{5} \\\\ N & =2\\,609\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={5n-620:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 2\\,609}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $2\\,609$ elements, we must have $|A|=2\\,609.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306115 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebc025a5-9c66-5ddc-a12c-42595f905c17" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Geometric Sequences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b34cd758-ad00-511f-b62f-2288203de635" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306117} {:answer/id #uuid "05ce2efe-1704-5dad-a131-8dd0858ff065" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370063}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b34cd758-ad00-511f-b62f-2288203de635" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306117} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b2196f8-084b-5bf3-a44f-def1c362bf61" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306116}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b7c6f1d2-1982-573c-ba1d-3b71c29477d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-181576" :question/problem "If $A={2,10,50,250,…,2\\,441\\,406\\,250},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n2,\\,10,\\,50,\\,250,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =5 \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{50}{10} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our geometric sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1}=2({5}^{n-1})=\\frac{2}{5}(5)^{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nA={\\frac{2}{5}(5)^{n}:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}(5)^{N} & =2\\,441\\,406\\,250 \\\\ {5}^{N} & =6\\,103\\,515\\,625 \\\\ N & ={log}_{5}⁡(6\\,103\\,515\\,625) \\\\ N & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡(6\\,103\\,515\\,625)}{{log}_{10}⁡(5)} \\\\ N & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={\\frac{2}{5}(5)^{n}:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 14}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $14$ elements, we must have $|A|=14.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306122 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebc025a5-9c66-5ddc-a12c-42595f905c17" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Geometric Sequences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e023ebb9-f5d9-503a-a18e-f06bd6ea2fe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306124}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e023ebb9-f5d9-503a-a18e-f06bd6ea2fe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306124} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac30c343-541b-548d-bae1-0ef841ae60de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306123}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "22256f74-ecc6-5ea7-b1e4-d18dff2b6d95" :question/math-academy-id "q-181582" :question/problem "If $A={1,6,36,216,…,2\\,176\\,782\\,336},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n1,\\,6,\\,36,\\,216,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=6:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =6 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{6} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our geometric sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1}=1\\cdot {6}^{n-1}={6}^{n-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nA={{6}^{n-1}:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{6}^{N-1} & =2\\,176\\,782\\,336 \\\\ N-1 & ={log}_{6}⁡(2\\,176\\,782\\,336) \\\\ N-1 & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡(2\\,176\\,782\\,336)}{{log}_{10}⁡(6)} \\\\ N-1 & =12 \\\\ N & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={{6}^{n-1}:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 13}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $13$ elements, we must have $|A|=13.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306125 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebc025a5-9c66-5ddc-a12c-42595f905c17" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Geometric Sequences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3ff0e5d-b30f-5eb8-ba83-b400e6c1c76f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306127}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3ff0e5d-b30f-5eb8-ba83-b400e6c1c76f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306127} :answer-field/id #uuid "f290bfa4-b622-5f4d-8879-13eb7efca3a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306126}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b40818b3-dded-5ed0-bad5-7f30d36c8460" :question/math-academy-id "q-181583" :question/problem "If $A={1,11,121,1\\,331,…,214\\,358\\,881},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n1,\\,11,\\,121,\\,1\\,331,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=11:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =11 \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{121}{11} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our geometric sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1}=1\\cdot {11}^{n-1}={11}^{n-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nA={{11}^{n-1}:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{11}^{N-1} & =214\\,358\\,881 \\\\ N-1 & ={log}_{11}⁡(214\\,358\\,881) \\\\ N-1 & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡(214\\,358\\,881)}{{log}_{10}⁡(11)} \\\\ N-1 & =8 \\\\ N & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={{11}^{n-1}:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 9}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $9$ elements, we must have $|A|=9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370064 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebc025a5-9c66-5ddc-a12c-42595f905c17" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Geometric Sequences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fdee566-24a5-5f52-9998-9b048b8c1813" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8fdee566-24a5-5f52-9998-9b048b8c1813" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370066} :answer-field/id #uuid "3718f2c2-13cf-55a6-baf5-30430ca76173" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370065}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b4b82edb-27c4-5eb4-8e21-16aeb96703eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-181584" :question/problem "If $A={1,9,81,729,…,3\\,486\\,784\\,401},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n1,\\,9,\\,81,\\,729,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=9:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =9 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{9} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our geometric sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1}=1\\cdot {9}^{n-1}={9}^{n-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nA={{9}^{n-1}:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{9}^{N-1} & =3\\,486\\,784\\,401 \\\\ N-1 & ={log}_{9}⁡(3\\,486\\,784\\,401) \\\\ N-1 & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡(3\\,486\\,784\\,401)}{{log}_{10}⁡(9)} \\\\ N-1 & =10 \\\\ N & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={{9}^{n-1}:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 11}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $11$ elements, we must have $|A|=11.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054996 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "24ce056e-1fe1-55d4-b88c-62629435003b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cardinality of a Set With Set Elements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "854b829e-2514-5d23-8490-af95e11bd964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "854b829e-2514-5d23-8490-af95e11bd964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370067} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f14371e-b216-5a35-a5f5-0b0056fdbe9a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051864}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f6645ea0-8c36-5c97-b3b4-764e97533b77" :question/math-academy-id "q-181587" :question/problem "If $X={{1,2,3,4,5},{1,2,3,4},∅}$, then $|X|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $X$ is the number of elements in $X.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $X:$\n\n$$\n{1,2,3,4,5},\\,{1,2,3,4},\\,∅\n$$\n\nNote that ${1,2,3,4,5},$ ${1,2,3,4},$ and $∅$ each count as single elements of $X.$\n\nSince $X$ has $3$ elements, the cardinality is $|X|=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370068 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb35fcff-d9f0-5ae8-999e-7e8bbc0b0919" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cardinality of a Finite Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6444c6f9-6346-5e12-95e0-7f0673921649" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370070} {:answer/id #uuid "a3713be0-b7a2-5949-806b-1ddc3f66004e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370071} {:answer/id #uuid "c4bad949-30c7-558f-93ca-179cb262af76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370072} {:answer/id #uuid "4b137b24-202f-5c12-b93f-edc01961b5ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370073} {:answer/id #uuid "0e05f542-a3ea-5acf-875b-a27896151c88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e05f542-a3ea-5acf-875b-a27896151c88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370074} :answer-field/id #uuid "2738121f-3a00-57a6-bcdc-27c9f978270b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370069}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "20c4225d-0d81-5ff8-857a-87c9bd75e2a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-36915" :question/problem "If $C={♣,♠,♡,♢,△,♣}$, then $|C|=$" :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $C$ is the number of elements in $C.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $C:$\n\n$$\n♣,\\,♠,\\,♡,\\,♢,\\,△\n$$\n\nNote that only *unique* elements are counted. In other words, duplicate elements are *not* counted separately.\n\nSince $C$ has $5$ elements, its cardinality is $|C|=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370075 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "24ce056e-1fe1-55d4-b88c-62629435003b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cardinality of a Set With Set Elements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ae26c5f-8915-5625-9445-0025187f80d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370077} {:answer/id #uuid "58edd90d-8901-5d02-ab61-cf9eb51d8bbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370078} {:answer/id #uuid "108c8d4b-ca23-5fc2-843b-dec32eca569b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370079} {:answer/id #uuid "32eb2c48-d108-52ed-9271-8252e98acc6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370080} {:answer/id #uuid "1e1ff813-942e-521